��i<?php exit; ?>a:2:{s:7:"content";O:8:"stdClass":24:{s:2:"ID";i:5348;s:11:"post_author";s:1:"1";s:9:"post_date";s:19:"2026-04-01 09:57:01";s:13:"post_date_gmt";s:19:"2026-04-01 09:57:01";s:12:"post_content";s:1359:"<blockquote class="blog-details__blockquote"><p>Remote work that lasts protects maker time, measures outcomes instead of hours online, and rotates the cost of late meetings.</p></blockquote><figure class="blog-details__figure wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://nsc.test/wp-content/themes/NSC-Software/frontend/build/img/blog7.webp" alt="Company Anniversary: Lessons from Growth — team collaboration" loading="lazy" width="1200" height="675" /></figure><p>If you are planning a similar initiative, start with a thin end-to-end slice, instrument it in production, and expand scope only when telemetry supports the next bet.</p><ol class="blog-details__list"><li>Interview alumni for honest lessons</li><li>Invest profits into tooling debt</li><li>Tell failure stories, not only wins</li></ol><p>NSC marks milestones by publishing internal playbooks we wish we had on day one: onboarding, escalation, and how we say no politely.</p><p>Growth without guardrails creates accidental specialization silos where only two people understand the billing subsystem.</p><p>Anniversaries tempt vanity metrics—headcount charts and office photos. The useful retrospective asks which bets paid off, which clients stayed, and which processes we would never repeat.</p><h3 class="blog-details__h3">Handover checklist we use</h3><hr class="blog-details__divider" />";s:10:"post_title";s:40:"Company Anniversary: Lessons from Growth";s:12:"post_excerpt";s:317:"Company Anniversary: Lessons from Growth — Anniversaries tempt vanity metrics—headcount charts and office photos. The useful retrospective asks which bets paid off, which clients stayed, and which processes we would never repeat. Growth without guardrails creates accidental specialization silos where only two…";s:11:"post_status";